{"id": "EUVD-2026-55605", "enisaUuid": "bfa4dcf6-0ee8-3d6d-a48d-c324b5cdb6c7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/irdma: Prevent rereg_mr for non-mem regions\n\nWhen a QP/CQ/SRQ is created, a two step process is used\nwhere the buffer is allocated in userspace and explicitly\nregistered with the normal reg_mr mechanism prior to creating\nthe actual QP/CQ/SRQ object.\n\nThese special registrations are indicated via an ABI field\nso the driver knows that they do not have a valid mkey and\nto skip the actual CQP command submission.\n\nSince these are real MR objects from the core's perspective,\nit is possible for a user application to invoke rereg_mr on them\nand cause a real CQP op to be emitted with the zero-initialized\nmkey value of 0.\n\nFix this by preventing rereg_mr on these special regions.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:09:09", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fb46d134e1b8690bed2da9005b36d32d2efd34ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5029e91c63406e4f4c8d58161048b41b6f0bd8c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca1c29f05274b737dc964e28b97803750d7cf7ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbaa37e060918c45517786e37ecab0f300b48fa9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a846aecb931b4d65d5eafa92a0623545af46d4f2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-68419", "GHSA-f527-f42m-rc5q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0078d96a-45bd-3067-bb99-fe8d75fb079e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "1f2b20f0-8c0e-3a49-9e8a-df3567e12e6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.120 <6.6.148"}, {"id": "4fa5f84d-c78b-3024-a97b-f3f47cb91ad1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "64e63ae0-71a0-3621-ad24-8d620d8d89ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "715fdb3b30541cc8180b7cdc6aa9f8c307afdf25 <fb46d134e1b8690bed2da9005b36d32d2efd34ac"}, {"id": "6dc24aa7-14af-3b2b-a9dd-e7f7daba62e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "73c1a0d3-94e6-3258-bdb8-ad9958d70159", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <a846aecb931b4d65d5eafa92a0623545af46d4f2"}, {"id": "90f1f6d8-f56d-32ba-ab92-f1bcbea8a23b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <ca1c29f05274b737dc964e28b97803750d7cf7ec"}, {"id": "a97e0f42-3514-3207-b3e4-39ceffa419ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "b4ff9161-760e-30fb-81d8-31401908e521", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <b5029e91c63406e4f4c8d58161048b41b6f0bd8c"}, {"id": "bf0e63b0-d763-3ed0-beb3-8d21af5e6d7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac388db27c443dadfbb0b8b23fa7ccf429d901a <dbaa37e060918c45517786e37ecab0f300b48fa9"}, {"id": "c8a5d798-ea34-3261-a51d-d3e7ca617ce5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dfe472d2-6825-327a-97bb-12ae1da44df6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "f38742e8-d768-3f55-9857-143f8041bdce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6203b92a-173f-3a73-b756-deb0ab94a793", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}